# Guardentra — master project architecture rules

## Backend / Cloud Run / Firebase App Hosting

- Backend configurations must always read the dynamic environment port variable via `process.env.PORT || 8080` and explicitly bind to network host `0.0.0.0`.
- Never hardcode ports 3000 or 5000, as this triggers Firebase App Hosting container startup timeouts.

## Branch architecture

- Keep repository branches isolated, but never equate a branch push with environment deployment authority. Protected `main` is the release source branch; staging/production promotion requires the current issue-bound release packet, exact environment readback, and rollback evidence. P0 #126 currently proves that a main push can also trigger an unintended legacy backend rollout, so branch name alone is never deployment truth.

## Firebase environments

- Demo/legacy project `guardentra-7f582` is not staging or production. Named release environments are `guardentra-staging` and `guardentra-prod`; use explicit environment-scoped packets and never rely on the Firebase default alias (see `docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md`).
- Client must use `VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY` (and optional other `VITE_FIREBASE_*`); demo `firebase-applet-config.json` holds non-secret project identifiers only — never commit live Web API keys (see `docs/SECRETS.md`).
